// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Serverless database bootstrap (F-01 mitigation, V8).
//
// Problem: on Vercel, a SQLite `file:` DATABASE_URL created at build time does
// not ship inside the serverless bundle, so every DB-backed API fails with
// "unable to open the database file" (the deployed /api/v1/health reports
// database: fail).
//
// Mitigation: embed a pristine schema + synthetic-seed database (the exact
// output of `prisma db push` + `bun prisma/seed.ts` — clearly-labeled demo
// data only, no real user data) as base64. At cold start, when running on
// Vercel with a `file:` DATABASE_URL and no durable database configured, it
// is written to /tmp/banglashield.db and used from there. /tmp is the only
// writable path in a serverless function.
//
// Honest limitation (documented in README "Known serverless limitation"):
// data is PER-INSTANCE and resets on cold start — visitors' analyses and
// reports are not durable. Setting DATABASE_URL to a hosted database (e.g.
// PostgreSQL) bypasses this bootstrap entirely and is the production path.
//
// Regenerate after a schema or seed change (see docs/V8-RELEASE-QA.md):
//   rm -f prisma/demo-seed.db
//   DATABASE_URL="file:./demo-seed.db" bunx prisma db push --skip-generate
//   DATABASE_URL="file:../prisma/demo-seed.db" bun prisma/seed.ts
//   python3 tools/embed-demo-db.py
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
